`TypeInfo_Class.vtbl` and `Interface.vtbl` have been removed

These opaque `void*[]` tables are hardly useful and have been removed to make
class TypeInfos slightly leaner, and prepare for generating the TypeInfo in
library code.

If really needed, the pointer to the vtable of a class (the vptr) is stored at
the start of each class instance, including init symbol. E.g.:

```
// for a dynamic type:
immutable(void*)* vptr = myObject.__vptr;
// for a static type:
immutable(void*)* vptr = *cast(immutable(void*)**) __traits(initSymbol, MyClass).ptr;
```
